"""Build the public, dependency-free support/legal site. No account data is embedded."""
from pathlib import Path
import html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'website'
BASE='/Beamlet/'
EMAIL='hasaamb@gmail.com'
content={
'':('Beamlet — Remote Control, within reach.', '''<h1>Remote Control.<br>Within reach.</h1><p class="lead">Start, monitor, and stop Claude Code Remote Control from your Mac menu bar.</p><div class="card"><strong>Free and open source.</strong><p>Beamlet is in development. The source is available under the MIT license. A Mac App Store release is not yet available.</p><a href="https://github.com/BlockchainHB/Beamlet">View the source on GitHub →</a></div><h2>A small home for your connection</h2><p>See whether Remote Control is starting, online, reconnecting or needs attention. When connected, open Claude or use the connection link to continue on another device.</p><p>Choose your starting folder and optional startup, power and notification preferences. After initial setup, Beamlet manages the connection without a terminal window dedicated to it.</p><h2>What you need</h2><p>The current version requires a compatible Claude Code installation, an account eligible for Remote Control, and completed sign-in, workspace trust and consent. Your Mac must stay powered on and connected to the internet.</p><div class="links"><a href="support/">Setup and support</a><a href="privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="terms/">Terms of use</a></div>'''),
'privacy':('Beamlet Privacy Policy', '''<h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="date">Effective September 23, 2026 · Maintained by HASAAM MANZOOR BHATTI</p><p>This policy describes Beamlet, an independent macOS utility for managing Claude Code Remote Control, and this support website.</p><h2>Information on your Mac</h2><p>Beamlet stores preferences such as your starting folder, installed executable path, startup options and notification choices locally. Sandboxed builds also store security-scoped bookmarks for files and folders you select. Local lock files coordinate the process Beamlet starts.</p><p>Beamlet processes CLI output in memory to determine connection state and read the connection link. It keeps a bounded, in-memory history of connection diagnostic events. Diagnostics redact common secret, URL and home-folder patterns, but redaction is not a guarantee that every sensitive value is removed.</p><h2>What Beamlet sends</h2><p>Beamlet does not operate an account backend, include an advertising or analytics integration, or automatically upload connection diagnostics to its publisher in the current implementation.</p><p>If you choose Copy connection link or Copy diagnostics, that content goes to your system clipboard. A connection QR code represents the session link. Opening a connection opens Claude in your browser. Treat connection links and QR codes as private.</p><h2>Claude Code and third parties</h2><p>Claude Code handles its own authentication, AI processing and Remote Control network traffic. Beamlet uses your installed CLI; it does not collect your Claude password through a Beamlet login form. We do not claim that prompts, code, conversations or other Claude activity remain entirely on your Mac.</p><p>Review <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic’s privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/data-usage">Claude Code’s data documentation</a>. Their terms and practices apply to their services.</p><h2>Software updates</h2><p>The App Store build configuration contains no separate update service. The development/direct-distribution version includes Sparkle, whose update checks are inactive unless an update feed is configured. If enabled in a future direct release, requests to the update host may expose standard network information such as your IP address and requested version. This policy will identify that service before release.</p><h2>Permissions and control</h2><p>Notifications, launch at login, automatic connection and keep-awake behavior are optional. Change them in Beamlet or macOS System Settings. Closing Settings leaves the menu-bar utility running; quitting Beamlet requests shutdown of its own managed process.</p><p>Uninstalling Beamlet does not delete Claude Code, its account data or your projects. Preferences and support files can remain on your Mac. Contact us for removal instructions appropriate to your installed version.</p><h2>This website and support</h2><p>This site uses GitHub Pages and has no added analytics, advertising scripts or tracking cookies. GitHub may process technical request information to provide and protect its hosting service; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p><p>If you email support, we receive your email address and the content you send through our email provider, Gmail. We use that information to answer your request and maintain support correspondence as needed. You can request deletion by emailing us; applicable legal obligations may require some records to be retained. Do not send credentials, live session links or private source code. Public GitHub issues are visible to others and are also subject to GitHub’s policies.</p><h2>Contact and changes</h2><p>For privacy questions or data requests, contact HASAAM MANZOOR BHATTI at <a href="mailto:hasaamb@gmail.com">hasaamb@gmail.com</a>. We will update this page and its effective date when our practices change.</p>'''),
'terms':('Beamlet Terms of Use', '''<h1>Terms of use</h1><p class="date">Effective September 23, 2026 · HASAAM MANZOOR BHATTI</p><p>Beamlet is an independent utility for managing a Claude Code Remote Control process on your Mac. These terms explain the project’s licensing, scope and support. They do not create an account, subscription or payment obligation.</p><h2>Open-source license</h2><p>Beamlet’s source is provided under the <a href="https://github.com/BlockchainHB/Beamlet/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT License</a>. That license grants broad rights to use, copy, modify and distribute the software, subject to retaining its copyright and permission notice. These terms do not restrict those MIT rights. Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.</p><h2>App Store copies</h2><p>No Mac App Store release is currently available. If Beamlet is subsequently distributed through the Mac App Store without a custom license agreement, Apple’s <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a> applies to that store distribution, alongside applicable Apple terms and your statutory rights.</p><h2>Third-party requirements</h2><p>Claude Code and Remote Control are provided by Anthropic, not Beamlet. The current implementation requires you to install and configure Claude Code and have an eligible account. Beamlet does not include or sell a Claude subscription, grant rights to Anthropic services or bypass their permissions, consent or usage policies. Availability may change when third-party software or services change.</p><h2>Your use</h2><p>Use Beamlet only with computers, files and accounts you are authorized to access. You remain responsible for selecting the workspace, reviewing Claude’s permissions and instructions, and the actions performed through your remote session. Keep credentials and connection links private and maintain suitable backups.</p><p>Your Mac must remain powered on and connected to the internet. Beamlet does not guarantee uninterrupted connections, closed-lid operation or successful recovery from every failure.</p><h2>Warranty and liability</h2><p>The MIT-licensed software is provided “as is,” without warranties, subject to the MIT License’s warranty disclaimer and limitation of liability. Nothing on this page excludes rights or liabilities that applicable law does not allow to be excluded.</p><h2>Privacy and support</h2><p>Our <a href="../privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains local data handling, third-party services and support correspondence. Contact <a href="mailto:hasaamb@gmail.com">hasaamb@gmail.com</a> for help or questions about these terms. Support is offered on a best-effort basis.</p><h2>Independence</h2><p>Beamlet is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Anthropic or Apple. References to Claude Code and macOS describe compatibility.</p>'''),
'support':('Beamlet Support', '''<h1>How can we help?</h1><p class="lead">Contact <a href="mailto:hasaamb@gmail.com">hasaamb@gmail.com</a> or <a href="https://github.com/BlockchainHB/Beamlet/issues">open a GitHub issue</a>.</p><div class="card">Beamlet is in development. The App Store compatibility build is still being validated; it is not a released store app.</div><h2>Set up the current direct build</h2><ol><li>Install Claude Code from its <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup">official source</a> and confirm your account has Remote Control access.</li><li>Open Terminal in your project folder. Run <code>claude auth login</code> if you are not signed in.</li><li>Run <code>claude</code> in that folder and accept workspace trust. Complete Remote Control’s one-time consent when prompted.</li><li>Stop any Remote Control session you started manually before starting it in Beamlet.</li><li>In Settings → Connection, choose your starting folder and Claude Code executable. Press Start Remote Control.</li><li>Once Online, use Open in Claude, Copy connection link or Connect your phone.</li></ol><h2>Already signed in, but Beamlet asks for login?</h2><p>Check <code>command -v claude</code> and <code>claude auth status --json</code> in Terminal. Make sure Beamlet uses that installation and the account eligible for Remote Control. Do not send tokens or passwords to support.</p><h2>Stuck on Starting?</h2><p>Complete sign-in, workspace trust and Remote Control consent in Terminal first. Check your selected folder and internet connection. Organization policies or an unsupported CLI version can prevent Remote Control from starting.</p><h2>Does my Mac need to stay awake?</h2><p>Yes. Remote Control runs on your Mac. The optional keep-awake setting applies while the connection runs and the Mac is plugged in. Closing the lid can still cause sleep.</p><h2>What happens when I quit?</h2><p>Beamlet requests shutdown of its owned process. It does not intentionally stop unrelated terminal sessions. Closing the Settings window only closes that window.</p><h2>Report an issue safely</h2><p>Include your Beamlet, macOS and Claude Code versions, the steps to reproduce and the displayed error. About → Connection diagnostics lets you inspect and copy recent events. Review and redact anything you share; public GitHub issues are visible to everyone. Never include credentials, working connection links or private QR codes.</p><p>See <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/remote-control">Claude Code’s current Remote Control requirements</a> for supported accounts and configurations.</p>''')}
for route,(title,body) in content.items():
    nav=''.join(f'<a href="{BASE}{k}/"'+(' aria-current="page"' if k==route else '')+f'>{label}</a>' for k,label in [('support','Support'),('privacy','Privacy'),('terms','Terms')])
    doc=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Beamlet is a free, open-source Mac menu bar companion for Claude Code Remote Control."><title>{html.escape(title)}</title><link rel="canonical" href="https://blockchainhb.github.io{BASE}{route+'/' if route else ''}"><link rel="icon" href="{BASE}assets/beamlet.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="{BASE}assets/style.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a class="brand" href="{BASE}"><img src="{BASE}assets/beamlet.png" alt="" width="44" height="44">Beamlet</a><nav aria-label="Main">{nav}</nav></header><main id="main">{body}</main><footer><p>© 2026 HASAAM MANZOOR BHATTI and Beamlet contributors · <a href="https://github.com/BlockchainHB/Beamlet">MIT-licensed source</a></p><p>Independent companion. Not affiliated with Anthropic.</p></footer></body></html>'''
    target=ROOT/route/'index.html';target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);target.write_text(doc)
(ROOT/'.nojekyll').write_text('')
print('Built four static pages.')
